### MCP Resource Server — Test Requests
### Start the auth server first:  go run ./cmd/server/
### Start the resource server:    go run ./cmd/resource/
### Then run steps below in order.

### ────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Step 1: Check RFC 9728 metadata (no auth needed)
### Expected: 200, JSON with resource + authorization_servers
### ────────────────────────────────────────────────
GET http://localhost:8081/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource

### ────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Step 2: Try MCP without a token — must get 401
### Check the WWW-Authenticate header in the response:
###   Bearer realm="mcp-auth-poc", resource_metadata="http://localhost:8081/..."
### This is the MCP Auth discovery signal — clients follow resource_metadata.
### ────────────────────────────────────────────────
POST http://localhost:8081/mcp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 1,
  "method": "initialize",
  "params": {
    "protocolVersion": "2024-11-05",
    "capabilities": {},
    "clientInfo": {"name": "test-client", "version": "1.0"}
  }
}

### ────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Steps 3-6: Get a fresh access token first!
###
### Run the full PKCE flow from token.http (Steps 1-4),
### then paste the access_token value below.
### ────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Step 3: Initialize MCP session (with valid token)
### Expected: 200, protocolVersion + capabilities + serverInfo
POST http://localhost:8081/mcp
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 1,
  "method": "initialize",
  "params": {
    "protocolVersion": "2024-11-05",
    "capabilities": {},
    "clientInfo": {"name": "test-client", "version": "1.0"}
  }
}

### Step 4: List available tools
### Expected: 200, {"tools": [{"name": "echo", ...}, {"name": "current_time", ...}]}
POST http://localhost:8081/mcp
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 2,
  "method": "tools/list",
  "params": {}
}

### Step 5: Call the echo tool
### Expected: 200, {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Hello, MCP!"}]}
POST http://localhost:8081/mcp
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 3,
  "method": "tools/call",
  "params": {
    "name": "echo",
    "arguments": {"message": "Hello, MCP!"}
  }
}

### Step 6: Call the current_time tool
### Expected: 200, {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "2026-05-21T...Z"}]}
POST http://localhost:8081/mcp
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 4,
  "method": "tools/call",
  "params": {
    "name": "current_time",
    "arguments": {}
  }
}

### Step 7: Error case — unknown tool
### Expected: 200 with JSON-RPC error {"code": -32602, "message": "unknown tool: whoami"}
POST http://localhost:8081/mcp
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 5,
  "method": "tools/call",
  "params": {
    "name": "whoami",
    "arguments": {}
  }
}
